# 5. Security Controls

## Secret Detection

GitLeaks scans the repository for exposed credentials, including:

- API Keys
- Access Tokens
- Passwords
- Private Keys
- AWS Credentials
- GitHub Tokens

This prevents sensitive information from being committed to source control.

---

## Static Code Analysis

SonarCloud analyzes the application source code to identify:

- Bugs
- Security vulnerabilities
- Code smells
- Reliability issues
- Maintainability concerns
- Quality Gate compliance

Static analysis helps developers resolve issues before deployment.

---

## Filesystem Vulnerability Scanning

Trivy scans the application source directory before containerization.

The scan identifies:

- Vulnerable dependencies
- Operating system packages
- Language packages
- Known CVEs

---

## Container Image Scanning

After Docker images are built, Trivy performs image scanning to identify vulnerabilities contained within the final deployment artifact.

Security findings include:

- Critical vulnerabilities
- High vulnerabilities
- Medium vulnerabilities
- Low vulnerabilities

